AMDMIGraphX (pinned tag rocm-6.4.4): do not emit the gfx9 form of v_add_u32 for
integer DPP sums on gfx8.

WHY
---
src/targets/gpu/kernels/include/migraphx/kernels/reduce.hpp implements wave
reductions (dpp_reduce) with inline assembly that spells each step as
"<ins> %0 %0 %0 row_shr:N" and similar, one overload per element type and
operation. The int32_t and uint32_t overloads for op::sum use the instruction
name v_add_u32. gfx9 and later have a three-operand v_add_u32 with no carry
output; gfx8 only has the carry-out encoding, which takes an explicit vcc
operand, so the assembler rejects the string. Any reduction kernel that
instantiates dpp_reduce for an int32 or uint32 sum on gfx803 therefore fails to
compile:

    error: not a valid operand.

for the first asm statement, while the same source assembles for gfx900. The
failure is a kernel JIT error at model compile time, not a wrong result.
Floating-point sums (v_add_f32, v_add_f16, v_add_f64) assemble on gfx803.

WHAT
----
Split MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE into a floating-point part (MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_FLOAT)
and an integer part (MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_INT32), with the same overloads as
before, and on gfx8 (__GFX8__) define only the floating-point overloads for
op::sum. Integer sums then resolve to the generic dpp_reduce template at the top
of the file, which builds the same reduction from dpp_mov builtins and lets the
compiler choose the encoding of the add for the target. Every other architecture
and every other operation keeps the asm overloads unchanged. The marker
GFX803_DPP_INT32_SUM sits once in reduce.hpp.

VERIFICATION (RX 590, gfx803, image built with this patch): tools/correctness-suite/pytorch/migraphx_check.py compiles
reduce_sum over int32 and uint32 tensors (axes of 16, 64, 256, 1000 and 4096 elements) for the gpu target and compares
with numpy. Without the patch the int32 programs fail to compile ("not a valid operand" at the DPP add); with it all
ten cases are exact. The compile matrix (hipcc with MIGraphX's JIT flags, gfx803 and gfx900) is as follows: the
unpatched header fails the two integer sums for gfx803 and builds the other 14 of 16; with -std=c++20 and no warning
flags, dpp_reduce<16> and <64> over sum, product, max and min for int32, uint32, float and half build for gfx803 and
gfx900 except the int32 and uint32 products, which fail on both architectures before and after the patch (v_mul_u32 is
not an instruction).

diff --git a/src/targets/gpu/kernels/include/migraphx/kernels/reduce.hpp b/src/targets/gpu/kernels/include/migraphx/kernels/reduce.hpp
index 76150cb..7be97b2 100644
--- a/src/targets/gpu/kernels/include/migraphx/kernels/reduce.hpp
+++ b/src/targets/gpu/kernels/include/migraphx/kernels/reduce.hpp
@@ -146,23 +146,34 @@ __device__ void dpp_reduce(T& in, Op op)
 // Navi21 doesn't support int32 dpp
 #if defined(__gfx1030__)
 // NOLINTNEXTLINE
-#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op, prefix, sign)              \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(double, op, prefix##_f64); \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(float, op, prefix##_f32);  \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(half, op, prefix##_f16);   \
+#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_INT32(op, prefix, sign) \
     MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(uint32_t, op, prefix##_u32);
 #else
 // NOLINTNEXTLINE
-#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op, prefix, sign)                   \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(double, op, prefix##_f64);      \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(float, op, prefix##_f32);       \
-    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(half, op, prefix##_f16);        \
+#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_INT32(op, prefix, sign)             \
     MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(int32_t, op, prefix##sign##32); \
     MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(uint32_t, op, prefix##_u32);
 #endif
 
+// NOLINTNEXTLINE
+#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_FLOAT(op, prefix)              \
+    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(double, op, prefix##_f64); \
+    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(float, op, prefix##_f32);  \
+    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_ASM_FUN(half, op, prefix##_f16);
+
+// NOLINTNEXTLINE
+#define MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op, prefix, sign) \
+    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_FLOAT(op, prefix)     \
+    MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_INT32(op, prefix, sign)
+
 // Note: when max and min are in int32_t, signed version of instruction needs to be used.
+// GFX803_DPP_INT32_SUM: gfx8 only has the carry-out encoding of v_add_u32 (it takes a vcc operand), which
+// the three-operand DPP asm above cannot spell, so the integer sums use the generic dpp_mov path there.
+#if defined(__GFX8__)
+MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE_FLOAT(op::sum, v_add)
+#else
 MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op::sum, v_add, _u)
+#endif
 MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op::product, v_mul, _u)
 MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op::max, v_max, _i)
 MIGRAPHX_DPP_REDUCE(op::min, v_min, _i)
